Z||000009||Pontiaddict||11-24-2001||06:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>Is the stripe strictly for looks, or does it have another purpose?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They were first designes as autocross tires that had the colored stripe on the edges so the drivers could see how hard they were pushing the limits of the tires and if they were over/underinflated. But that idea got scrapped and the colors ended up being more for show instead.<P>Anyone know if they make colored smoke? I think I remember hearing someone say that they did.||||reg||1
Z||000010||newfie||11-24-2001||06:44 PM||||I was workin with Michelin (BFGoodrich) when these were first introduced.  I remember the employees got the first oppurtunity to get a set.  You can custom make your tires to have up to 2 colors over three treads.  There was a big demand for them, Very limited in sizes though, at least they were only available in 17's or 18's.  Heres a link<P>https://customcolor.bfgoodrichtires.com/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/ExecMacro/ScorcherTAOnline/frames.d2w/report?||||reg||1
Z||000011||johnt671||11-24-2001||07:35 PM||||Read in the paper when these tires first came out that some cities wanted to ban them.  Seems like the gangbangers were putting the same colors on their cars as their gang colors, going into other gang's turf and leaving red, blue or yellow burn patches.  Then the other gang would retaliate by emptying a few 9 magazines.  Crazy stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Neverfinished||11-24-2001||08:10 PM||||Heys guys...<BR>I can't take a pic tonite but they are very cool indeed.<BR>They are a performance tire and stick like glue. But they are very expensive. Like 300 a tire! ouch! Also they are 22540R17's if anyone cares. Cool tire and they get alot of looks.<P>Also I would advise against getting the blue ones as they don't show up very well.<BR>My buddy has a blue set and you wont notice them that much...<BR>But maybe with a blue care that would help set them off... Whatever floats your boat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
